This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   Build the complete cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, implemented as the Angular application already scaffolded in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`). The stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. The work is split into tickets in `spec/tickets/` (01-movie-list, 02-auditorium-map, 03-seat-selection, 04-booking-summary, 05-checkout, 06-confirmation, 07-final-pass) which must be implemented **in order**. `spec/README.md` is stated to be the **complete** specification: I must not ask any questions, and where the spec is silent I should choose the simplest option that satisfies it. The task is only finished when **every ticket is done** and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. (This was the entirety of the user's message — there have been no further user messages since.)

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Nx 23 monorepo, Angular 22 standalone zoneless application (no NgModules, signal-based reactivity, `input()`/`output()`/`signal()`/`computed()`/`effect()`/`toSignal()`).
   - Angular Material 22 + CDK (already installed) — must be used for every button, text field, checkbox, toast, and datepicker; **`@angular/animations` is NOT installed** and must not be added, which rules out `provideAnimations()`/`provideAnimationsAsync()`.
   - Native Date adapter already provided (`provideNativeDateAdapter()`).
   - `json-server` 0.17.4 backend serving `db.json` at `http://localhost:3000`, with CORS enabled; endpoints for `/movies`, `/movies/:id`, `/screenings` (with `date`/`movieId` query filters), `/screenings/:id`, and `POST /reservations`.
   - Booking state persisted in `sessionStorage`, modeled as a single `Booking` object (screeningId, seats[], paid, customerEmail, form).
   - CSS Grid-based auditorium layout with precomputed static geometry and an explicit column-track mapping function (`gridTrack`) to guarantee cross-row alignment regardless of which blocks exist in a given row (handles the "entrance" gap in rows 1–10).
   - Seat vs. couch identifier model: `R<row>C<column>` strings; couches (row 15) always toggled/stored as a pair of two identifiers.
   - Reactive Forms with custom validators and a cross-field "confirm email" validator that re-validates when the sibling control changes.
   - Angular Router functional guards (`CanActivateFn`) for booking-state-gated routes.
   - `data-testid` contract (section 9 of the spec) — exact attribute names/values are part of the contract and must not be renamed/abbreviated.
   - Vitest for unit tests, ESLint (`@nx/eslint:lint`) for linting, `@angular/build:application` esbuild-based builder for production build.
   - Environment networking quirk discovered: this sandbox's `localhost` sometimes resolves/binds inconsistently between IPv4 (`127.0.0.1`) and IPv6 (`::1`) across different Bash tool invocations — not an application issue.
   - No browser-automation tooling (chromium-cli, playwright, puppeteer) is installed as an npm package in this project, though a Playwright-downloaded Chromium binary happens to exist on disk at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome`.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`spec/README.md`, `spec/stack.md`, `spec/tickets/*.md`** — read in full; these are the complete, authoritative specification and ticket breakdown. Not modified.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models/movie.model.ts`** (created):
     ```ts
     export interface Movie {
       id: number;
       title: string;
       genre: string;
       runtimeMinutes: number;
       format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles';
     }
     ```

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models/screening.model.ts`** (created):
     ```ts
     export interface Screening {
       id: number;
       movieId: number;
       date: string;
       time: string;
       occupiedSeats: string[];
     }
     ```

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models/reservation.model.ts`** (created): `ReservationCustomer`, `ReservationRequest`, `Reservation extends ReservationRequest { id: number }`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models/booking.model.ts`** (created): `BookingForm`, `Booking`, `emptyBookingForm()`, `emptyBooking(screeningId)`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/utils/seat.util.ts`** (created) — core seat/pricing logic: `seatId`, `parseSeatId`, `isAccessible`, `couchPairs`, `couchPairFor`, `seatPrice`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`, `formatPrice`, `seatState`, `couchState`, `SummaryEntry` + `buildSummaryEntries`, `RowSelectionLine` + `buildRowSelectionLines`, `MAX_SEATS_PER_BOOKING=10`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/utils/date.util.ts`** (created, later edited) — `formatIso`, `isoToday`, `startOfToday` (added later), `parseIso`, `addDays`, `weekdayName`, `monthShort`, `formatShowDate`, `resolveSelectedDate`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/utils/auditorium-layout.util.ts`** (created) — `SeatCellVm`, `CouchCellVm`, `CellVm`, `RowVm`, `gridTrack(column)`, `buildAuditoriumLayout()`, exported constant `AUDITORIUM_LAYOUT`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/services/api.service.ts`** (created) — `ApiService` with `getMovies`, `getMovie`, `getScreeningsByDate`, `getScreening`, `createReservation`, base URL `http://localhost:3000`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/services/booking.service.ts`** (created) — signal-backed `BookingService` persisting to `sessionStorage` key `cinescope.booking`; methods `ensureForScreening`, `isActiveFor`, `isPaid`, `toggleSeats`, `removeSeats`, `updateForm`, `markPaid`, `clear`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/toast/toast.component.ts`** (created) — `ToastComponent`, `<span data-testid="toast">{{ message }}</span>`, reads `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/services/toast.service.ts`** (created) — `ToastService.show(message)` dismisses then opens via `MatSnackBar.openFromComponent(ToastComponent, {...duration: 4000})`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/core/guards/booking.guard.ts`** (created) — `activeBookingGuard`, `paidBookingGuard`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/day-picker.component.ts`** (created, edited to fix lint):
     Final relevant snippet:
     ```ts
     import { addDays, formatIso, parseIso, startOfToday, weekdayName } from '../../core/utils/date.util';
     ...
     export class DayPickerComponent {
       readonly selectedDate = input.required<string>();
       readonly dateSelected = output<string>();

       private readonly today = startOfToday();
       readonly minDate = this.today;

       readonly days: DayOption[] = Array.from({ length: 5 }, (_, i) => {
         const date = addDays(this.today, i);
         return { iso: formatIso(date), label: i === 0 ? 'Today' : weekdayName(date) };
       });

       readonly isDayButtonSelected = (iso: string) => this.selectedDate() === iso;

       readonly datepickerValue = computed(() => {
         const iso = this.selectedDate();
         return this.days.some((d) => d.iso === iso) ? null : parseIso(iso);
       });

       selectDay(iso: string): void { this.dateSelected.emit(iso); }
       onDatepickerChange(date: Date | null): void {
         if (date) { this.dateSelected.emit(formatIso(date)); }
       }
     }
     ```
   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/day-picker.component.html`** and **`.scss`** (created) — `data-testid="day-picker"`, `day-button` (data-date, data-selected), `date-picker` (mat-form-field wrapping matInput + matDatepicker).

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/movie-list.component.ts`** (created) — page component with `toSignal`-derived `queryDate`, `selectedDate` computed via `resolveSelectedDate`, `loading`/`error`/`movies`/`screenings` signals, `cards` computed, `effect()`-driven `load()`, `retry()`, `selectDay()`, `openScreening()`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/movie-list/movie-list.component.html`** and **`.scss`** (created) — implements loading/error/empty/loaded states and all `data-testid`s from spec section 9.1.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-selection/auditorium.component.ts`** (created, edited to rename output):
     Final relevant snippet:
     ```ts
     export class AuditoriumComponent {
       readonly occupiedSeats = input.required<string[]>();
       readonly selectedSeats = input.required<string[]>();
       readonly seatToggle = output<string[]>();

       readonly rows = AUDITORIUM_LAYOUT;

       private readonly occupiedSet = computed(() => new Set(this.occupiedSeats()));
       private readonly selectedSet = computed(() => new Set(this.selectedSeats()));

       seatState(cell: SeatCellVm): SeatState { ... }
       couchState(cell: CouchCellVm): SeatState { ... }
       onSeatClick(cell: SeatCellVm): void {
         if (this.seatState(cell) === 'unavailable') return;
         this.seatToggle.emit([cell.id]);
       }
       onCouchClick(cell: CouchCellVm): void {
         if (this.couchState(cell) === 'unavailable') return;
         this.seatToggle.emit([cell.id1, cell.id2]);
       }
     }
     ```
   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-selection/auditorium.component.html`** (created) — renders screen bar + 15 rows each with left label, blockA/aisle/blockB/aisle/blockC/right label, using `[style.grid-column]` per cell computed from `gridTrack`.
   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-selection/auditorium.component.scss`** (created, edited) — 28-track CSS grid (`2.5em repeat(4, 2.4em) 4.8em repeat(16, 2.4em) 4.8em repeat(4, 2.4em) 2.5em`), state-color classes `.state-available`/`.state-selected`/`.state-unavailable`/`.state-accessible` with the exact spec hex colors; removed a leftover `grid-column: 1` on `.seat-row` and a `:last-of-type` hack (replaced by explicit inline `style="grid-column: 28"` on the right row-label in the template).

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-selection/legend.component.ts/.html/.scss`** (created) — static 4-item legend matching spec colors/labels/order.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-selection/selected-seats-panel.component.ts/.html/.scss`** (created) — `count` and `rowLines` computed signals via `buildRowSelectionLines`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/seat-selection/seat-selection.component.ts/.html/.scss`** (created, template edited to rename event binding) — page component; template's auditorium binding is now `(seatToggle)="onToggle($event)"` (previously `(toggle)`).

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/summary/summary.component.ts/.html/.scss`** (created) — summary page with `entries`, `total`, `totalText` computed; `remove`/`back`/`confirm` methods.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/checkout/checkout.component.ts`** (created, then cleaned up): initially included redundant custom `requiredValidator()`/`requiredTrueValidator()`/`minLengthValidator()` functions and a dead empty `effect()` block — all removed; final version uses Angular's built-in `Validators.required`/`Validators.minLength`/`Validators.requiredTrue` plus custom `emailPatternValidator`, `phonePatternValidator`, and an inline cross-field mismatch validator added via `confirmEmailControl.addValidators(...)`. Key remaining structure:
     ```ts
     const EMAIL_PATTERN = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
     const PHONE_PATTERN = /^\d{9}$/;
     const FIELD_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {
       firstName: 'First name', lastName: 'Last name', email: 'Email',
       confirmEmail: 'Confirm email', phone: 'Phone number',
     };
     function emailPatternValidator(control) { ... }
     function phonePatternValidator(control) { ... }

     export class CheckoutComponent {
       readonly form = this.fb.group({
         firstName: ['', [Validators.required, Validators.minLength(2)]],
         lastName: ['', [Validators.required, Validators.minLength(2)]],
         email: ['', [Validators.required, emailPatternValidator]],
         confirmEmail: ['', [Validators.required]],
         phone: ['', [phonePatternValidator]],
         terms: [false, [Validators.requiredTrue]],
       });
       readonly total = computed(...);
       readonly payButtonText = computed(() => (this.submitting() ? 'Processing…' : `Pay ${formatPrice(this.total())}`));

       constructor() {
         const emailControl = this.form.controls.email;
         const confirmEmailControl = this.form.controls.confirmEmail;
         confirmEmailControl.addValidators((control) => {
           if (!control.value) return null;
           return control.value === emailControl.value ? null : { mismatch: true };
         });
         emailControl.valueChanges.subscribe(() => confirmEmailControl.updateValueAndValidity());

         const savedForm = this.bookingService.booking()?.form;
         if (savedForm) { this.form.patchValue(savedForm, { emitEvent: false }); }

         this.form.valueChanges.subscribe((value) => {
           this.bookingService.updateForm(value as Partial<BookingForm>);
         });
       }

       onTermsChange(): void { this.form.controls.terms.markAsTouched(); }
       errorMessage(field): string { ... /* required > minlength > email > mismatch > phonePattern */ }
       termsErrorMessage(): string { ... }
       showError(field): boolean { return !!control && control.invalid && control.touched; }
       showTermsError(): boolean { ... }
       back(): void { ... }
       submit(): void {
         if (this.form.invalid) {
           this.form.markAllAsTouched();
           this.toast.show('The form contains errors');
           return;
         }
         // builds reservation payload from buildSummaryEntries(booking.seats), posts, markPaid + navigate on success, toast on failure
       }
     }
     ```
   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/checkout/checkout.component.html`** (created) — all 6 fields + labels + error divs + terms checkbox + back/pay buttons, matching section 9.4 `data-testid`s exactly. Pay button `[disabled]="submitting()"` only (not tied to form validity).
   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/checkout/checkout.component.scss`** (created).

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/features/confirmation/confirmation.component.ts/.html/.scss`** (created) — `email` computed, `continue()` clears booking and navigates to `/`.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts`** (rewritten) — final content shown in section 2 above, importing all 5 feature components and the two guards.

   - **`apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts`** (rewritten twice) — final version (after removing animations):
     ```ts
     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';
     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';
     import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';
     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';

     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {
       providers: [
         provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(),
         provideRouter(appRoutes),
         provideNativeDateAdapter(),
         provideHttpClient(),
       ],
     };
     ```

   - **`package.json`** (read only, not modified) — confirms `json-server`, Material/CDK/forms/router/rxjs as the only relevant deps; no `@angular/animations`.

   - **`db.json`** (read only, not modified, per explicit spec rule "Do not edit db.json by hand").

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Error**: `pnpm nx build cinescope` aborted with `ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY` (interactive confirmation required to recreate `node_modules`).
     **Fix**: re-ran with `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`, which triggered a full `pnpm install` (succeeded, with non-fatal `msgpackr-extract` native-build warnings due to missing Python — did not block the install or build).
   - **Error**: Build failed with `Could not resolve "@angular/animations/browser"` after I added `provideAnimationsAsync()` to `app.config.ts`. Root cause: `@angular/animations` is not installed in this workspace (confirmed empty via `ls node_modules/@angular/ | grep -i anim` and absent from `package.json`), and the spec explicitly forbids adding dependencies.
     **Fix**: Removed `provideAnimationsAsync()` (and the import) from `app.config.ts` entirely; did not substitute `provideAnimations()` or `provideNoopAnimations()` either, since both statically import the same missing `@angular/animations/browser` module. Build then succeeded.
   - **Lint error**: `@angular-eslint/no-output-native` on `AuditoriumComponent`'s `toggle` output (collides with native DOM `toggle` event).
     **Fix**: Renamed the output property from `toggle` to `seatToggle` in `auditorium.component.ts` (declaration + both `.emit()` calls, done via `sed`), and updated the template binding in `seat-selection.component.html` from `(toggle)="onToggle($event)"` to `(seatToggle)="onToggle($event)"`.
   - **Lint warning**: `@typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion` on `day-picker.component.ts` (`parseIso(isoToday())!`).
     **Fix**: Added `startOfToday(): Date` to `date.util.ts` (constructs today's `Date` directly, no parse/assert needed) and switched `day-picker.component.ts` to use it instead.
   - After both lint fixes: `pnpm nx lint cinescope` → `✔ All files pass linting`; `pnpm nx build cinescope` re-run → still succeeds with only the pre-existing non-fatal bundle-size **warning** (699.61 kB vs 500 kB warning budget, well under the 1 MB error budget).
   - **Environment networking quirk** (not a code bug): Background-started `pnpm api` (json-server) via plain `nohup ... &` appeared unreachable via `node -e "fetch('http://localhost:3000/...')"` from a *subsequent* Bash tool call (`ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3000`), even though the server log showed it running fine. Restarting via the Bash tool's `run_in_background: true` failed with `EADDRINUSE: address already in use ::1:3000` — proving the original process actually was alive but bound only to the IPv6 loopback (`::1`), not `127.0.0.1`. Switching the test fetch to `http://[::1]:3000/movies` succeeded and returned real movie JSON. This appears to be a sandbox/tool-call network-isolation artifact rather than an application defect; I have not attempted to "fix" it in app code (and should not, since the spec mandates `http://localhost:3000` as the base URL).
   - **No browser-automation tool available**: `chromium-cli` is not installed; `playwright`/`puppeteer` npm packages are not installed in this project (`require.resolve` fails for both) and must not be added as dependencies per spec. However, a Playwright-downloaded Chromium **binary** does exist on disk at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome`, discovered via filesystem search, which could potentially be driven directly via the Chrome DevTools Protocol or via a globally-installed `playwright-core` package if one exists — I was actively searching for a global `playwright-core` installation (via `npm root -g` and a `find` across pnpm global stores) when the conversation was cut off for this summary; that search had so far returned no matches.

5. Problem Solving:
   - Designed a from-scratch Angular architecture satisfying the entire 675-line spec in one coherent pass (models/utils/services/guards/features), rather than ticket-by-ticket incremental delegation, judging the spec detailed enough to implement directly while still tracking ticket boundaries conceptually.
   - Solved the CSS-grid alignment problem for the auditorium (rows 1–10 missing the left "entrance" block, row 15 all-couches, two aisles, global column numbering) using a single `gridTrack(column)` mapping function shared by a static `AUDITORIUM_LAYOUT` precomputation, applied via inline `[style.grid-column]` per cell — this guarantees column 12 (etc.) aligns identically across every row regardless of which blocks that row's content list actually contains, without relying on DOM child order.
   - Solved couch-vs-seat duality (a couch contributes two seat identifiers that must always move together) via `couchPairFor(column)` / `buildSummaryEntries` / `buildRowSelectionLines`, all deduping on the couch's lower-numbered identifier so a couch is never double-counted or split.
   - Solved the "pay button always enabled except mid-request" requirement (AC-46) by explicitly decoupling the button's `[disabled]` binding from form validity — it's bound only to the `submitting()` signal.
   - Solved the "@angular/animations missing" constraint by dropping Material's animation providers entirely rather than attempting to add the dependency (forbidden by spec) — build succeeds without it; **runtime behavior of Material components without any animation provider has not yet been visually verified** (flagged as outstanding work).
   - Currently troubleshooting: how to actually run/drive the app in a browser for manual QA given the complete absence of browser-automation tooling in this sandbox, while respecting the "do not add dependencies" constraint (which arguably applies to the *project's* package.json, though I have not yet decided definitively whether installing a dev-only tool like `playwright-core` globally/temporarily for my own verification would be acceptable — this needs more thought or a pragmatic fallback to code review + unit tests if no viable browser path exists).

6. All user messages:
   - The original and only user message in this conversation:
     "Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds."
   - No further user messages have been sent since. (All subsequent content in the transcript consists of my own tool calls/outputs, system reminders, and one automated background-task failure notification — none of these are user input and none constitute approval, confirmation, or new instructions from the user.)

7. Pending Tasks:
   - Finish verifying/implementing all remaining ticket acceptance criteria end-to-end (tickets 01–07), including the ticket 07 "final pass" walk-through against every AC-01 through AC-69 and the full `data-testid` contract in section 9.
   - Attempt to actually run the app in a browser (dev server `pnpm nx serve cinescope` on port 4200 + backend `pnpm api` on port 3000) and visually/interactively verify the golden path and edge cases, per the standing project instruction: "For UI or frontend changes, start the dev server and use the feature in a browser before reporting the task as complete... Type checking and test suites verify code correctness, not feature correctness - if you can't test the UI, say so explicitly rather than claiming success." If no viable browser-automation path is found, I must explicitly tell the user that UI testing wasn't possible rather than claiming the UI was verified.
   - Run `pnpm nx test cinescope` (Vitest) to confirm the existing test suite still passes, and consider adding targeted unit tests for the trickiest pure logic (`seat.util.ts`, `date.util.ts`, `booking.service.ts`) to compensate for the lack of browser testing.
   - Re-confirm `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds as the final gating check once all other work is done.
   - Double check Material components render/behave acceptably without any animations provider (since `@angular/animations` could not be installed) — e.g., does `MatSnackBar`/`MatDatepicker`/`MatCheckbox` throw any runtime error or warning in the browser console without `provideAnimations()`/`provideNoopAnimations()`?
   - Verify the exact text-content purity requirements from spec section 9.7 (e.g., `seat` contains only its column number, `selected-seats-count` contains only its line, `summary-item-price` contains only the price, etc.) by inspecting rendered DOM, not just template source — ideally via an actual browser/DOM dump rather than code review alone.

8. Current Work:
